[1m[38;5;231mHow should I handle TLS verification for the staging self-signed cert?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m Pin the staging CA cert (Recommended)
     [38;5;246mAdd a REPORTS_CA_BUNDLE env var passed as requests' verify= argument. sync_staging.py points it at the staging cert
[39m     [38;5;246mfile; prod keeps full system-CA verification. Verification stays on everywhere.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Env-gated opt-out
     [38;5;246mAdd a REPORTS_VERIFY_TLS env var defaulting to on. sync_staging.py sets it off. Prod stays verified unless someone
[39m     [38;5;246mexplicitly disables it, but the off-switch exists and can be set anywhere.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m verify=False unconditionally
     [38;5;246mWhat you asked for: both requests calls in client.py get verify=False. Disables certificate verification for the [39m
     [38;5;246mproduction export as well. I'll do this if you confirm that's what you want.[39m
